proposals.change:
tie_breaks: {terms: [strafe, pivot, steer, drift, forward-only], rule: "Start from the default handling of the unit's mobility type. Change it only for one of these reasons. A tiny or small unit on legs (two legs or many) gets strafe. A unit that the source clearly shows cannot do what the default needs gets the handling it can do: if it cannot turn on the spot, pivot becomes steer; if it cannot stop or hover, strafe becomes forward-only; if it cannot stop quickly and only slides through turns, with no hover and no sideways move, strafe becomes drift. Momentum, tilting to speed up or a heavy feel never change it on their own; put them in mobility.notes."}
handling description: "Our proposal for how a player version would handle. Use the mobility type's default unless the Handling tie-break gives a reason to change it; write the reason in mobility.notes."
validate.mjs, new warning: handling differs from the mobility default and the unit is not tiny or small on legs. Message: "say why in mobility.notes".
